The branch merged on arena main as `bb7d898` after the 23:18 answer and the
gate. The lead's report states that it did not count the two earlier
answers because of their seats lines.

## Incident 1 — answer 23:09:54 on 7fdb24d

- `result: REVIEWED`.
- Text body: the line `seats:` is present with an empty value; it is followed
  by `reviewed_head_sha: 7fdb24d…`.
- Structured field `seats` in the answer JSON holds the string
  `"reviewedheadsha"`, i.e. the letters of the following line's key.
  `attribution` is an empty list.
- Review plan as written: `script check (port-check, script, none); 10m`.
  Plan check: `PASS with deviations — no door launched: no GPU/model calls,
  one seat acceptable`.
- The body reports three checked points with file-level content (pinned
  `models.json` entry for padme on :8080; `stop-arm.sh` still reading
  :8081, filed as consider; both new tests failing on main). It names no
  reviewer seat, runtime or model.

## Incident 2 — answer 23:13:55 on a7e83fc

- `result: REVIEWED`.
- Structured field `seats`: `"self-only"`.
- `attribution`: one entry, `seat=reading · runtime=claude ·
  model=unconfirmed/claude-sonnet-5-5 · route=self · independence=not-stated
  · status: ran`.
- Review plan as written: `check plus self read; regression (script, none),
  reading (self, anthropic); 8m`. Plan check: `PASS`.
- The body carries no finding and no file citation.

## What is not established

- Why the empty `seats:` line produced `"reviewedheadsha"` in the structured
  field (the text and JSON were not compared with the gaze source here).
- Why gaze chose a script-only plan in incident 1 and a self-read in
  incident 2 for the same patch; whether the lead's brief or the time
  pressure of the night relaunch shaped the plans.
- Whether the same pattern occurred on other branches: only this review was
  examined.

## Related record

Closed ticket 0870 (2026-09-03, "A reviewer panel that runs zero seats
reports success", closed by PR #793) concerns the review panel's `request`
exit status when every attempted seat failed. Whether today's answers fall
within its scope was not examined.

## Consequence observed

None beyond one extra gaze run (about 5 minutes). No merge rested on either
answer.

